<ArticleLayout
  title="GarageCloud vs Garage Hive | Comparison"
  description="How GarageCloud compares to Garage Hive: pricing, architecture and who each is built for. Garage Hive runs on Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central; GarageCloud is a standalone system."
  eyebrow="Comparison"
  breadcrumbLabel="GarageCloud vs Garage Hive"
  heading="GarageCloud vs Garage Hive"
  lede="Garage Hive is a Microsoft Dynamics 365 add-on with deep accounting depth. GarageCloud is a standalone system priced for smaller workshops."
>
  <p>
    <strong>The main difference is architecture, not features.</strong> Garage Hive is an add-on module built on top
    of Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central, not a standalone product. GarageCloud is a standalone system with no
    separate platform licence required.
  </p>

  <h2>Pricing</h2>
  <p>
    Garage Hive's published price starts from £145/month for the Garage Hive licence itself, but Business Central —
    the platform it runs on — carries its own Microsoft licence cost on top, currently around £61.50–£84.60 per
    user, per month. For a two-person workshop, the combined cost commonly starts around £268/month before setup.
    GarageCloud's Starter plan is £50/month, excluding VAT, with unlimited staff included
    (see <a href="https://garagehive.co.uk/pricing/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Garage Hive's pricing page</a> for their current published rates).
  </p>

  <h2>What Garage Hive does well</h2>
  <p>
    Because it sits on Business Central, Garage Hive gets genuine strengths from that platform: Power BI reporting,
    native Outlook and Teams integration, and deep accounting depth that a purpose-built garage tool would take
    years to match. For a workshop that's already committed to the Microsoft 365 ecosystem, or that needs
    enterprise-grade financial reporting, that's a real advantage.
  </p>

  <h2>What to weigh up</h2>
  <p>
    Some Garage Hive users have noted the combined licensing only makes financial sense with a team of six or more
    — a smaller, independent workshop can end up paying for Business Central capability it doesn't use. GarageCloud
    is built the other way round: a flat monthly fee per workshop, not per user, with no separate platform licence
    to manage.
  </p>

  <h2>Where GarageCloud is different, not necessarily better</h2>
  <p>
    GarageCloud is pre-launch, onboarding workshops from a waiting list. Garage Hive has an established customer
    base and a mature product. If deep Microsoft 365 integration is what a workshop needs today, Garage Hive already
    does that. If a workshop wants a standalone system without a Business Central licence attached, GarageCloud is
    built for that from the start — see <a href="/pricing">GarageCloud pricing</a>, or <a href="/garage-hive-alternatives">other Garage Hive alternatives</a>.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
